jobs.description:
Are you looking for a logistics job in the Beringe, Panningen, Helden, Meijel, Maasbree, Sevenum, Horst, Venlo, Roermond or Weert area? Then this is your chance to work for one of the world’s largest logistics employers. 
Whether you have experience as a logistics assistant, warehouse assistant, order picker, warehouse employee or production worker, or are looking to take your first steps in the logistics sector, we’d be happy to explore the possibilities with you.

- Order picking using a hand-held scanner;
- Collecting and processing orders;
- Packing and preparing products for dispatch;
- Sorting goods;
- Checking incoming and outgoing consignments;
- Loading and unloading lorries;
- Ensuring a safe, clean and organised working environment.

- Speak Dutch, English or German;
- Be motivated to work in logistics;
- Be able to work both independently and as part of a team;
- Work accurately and responsibly;
- Be available for day shifts or three-shift rotas;
- Be willing to carry out physical work;
- Have your own transport and accommodation (per candidate);
- Some experience in logistics would be an advantage;

As a Stock Control Officer, you are the guardian of our inventory and therefore a crucial link in the entire logistics process. Without you, everything comes to a standstill. 

De taken:

- Checking, analyzing, and correcting inventory discrepancies;
- Performing cycle counts and inventories;
- Identifying deviations and opportunities for improvement;
- Collaborating with warehouse staff and team leaders;
- Ensuring accurate administration in the system;
- You ensure that colleagues can rely on the correct quantities at the right time.

- You work accurately and have a strong sense of responsibility;
- You are stress-resistant and think in solutions;
- You speak and understand good English;
- You’re able to request a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are 18 years or older (due to working hours);
- You are willing to work in 2 shifts: 6:00 AM - 3:00 PM / 3:00 PM - 12:00 AM;
- You have an affinity for logistics and inventory management;
- Preferably experience with EPT, reach truck, or OPT
- Additionally, you have good knowledge of Microsoft Office, especially Microsoft Excel.
